  "title": "ldaneo: fix build on platforms without 128-bit division.",
  "description": "This is C, not C++, so you can't just use types, rather than formal\nparameters, for unused parameters in a function definition.  Visual\nStudio, for example, complains \"error C2055: expected formal parameter\nlist, not a type list\" for that.\n\nUse the parameter names and decorate them with `_U_` to indicate that\nthey're unused.",
